sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013) & Erlich et al. (2016) mollusc shell marginal buckling, hollow-spine closure and predator damage / mantle repair — Morphological realism / specimen match: 86/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The SHA-256-locked *Pecten jacobaeus* valve is still segmented to all 14 primary costae (`segment_pecten_specimen`, L1181-1265; dtheta = 9.40 deg, CV = 0.2196), and the Pass 3 3 x 3 synthesis figure plus the new 3D figure and 14-frame GIF render a recognisable hollow spine fold closing into a tube and a chipped valve healing back into register (L1267-1785, L1896-2033). Deductions: no Murex specimen is vendored, so the spine geometry (W = 6 mm, t = 0.35 mm, H/W at closure 2.31) is compared with nothing (-5); no repair-scar specimen or image is vendored, so the damage/repair trajectory is validated only against its own control (-4); the damaged-valve surface below the first station is a presentation-only linear amplitude ramp (L1051-1057) (-1); the Pecten segmentation uses a fixed `find_peaks` prominence/distance (L1232) tuned to this one image (-1); panel titles A/B/C overlap slightly in the 3 x 3 layout (pre-existing) (-1); the Pass 2 image evidence remains valid." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py L1037–L1070: build_damaged_valve_surface: chip notch for the figure; inner region below first station is a linear ramp (L1051-1057), presentation only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py#L1037-L1070>",
            "datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/README.md L1–L40: Only one specimen (Pecten jacobaeus valve) is vendored; no Murex spine or repair-scar specimen <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/README.md#L1-L40>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match-4> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.86"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match-1> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py L1181–L1265" ;
        dct:description "Polar DoG ridge segmentation of 14 primary radial costae; fixed find_peaks prominence 0.0018 / distance 22 at L1232" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py#L1181-L1265> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match-2> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py L1896–L2033" ;
        dct:description "render_pass3_3d_figure (hollow spine tube + chipped valve) and render_damage_repair_gif (14 frames)" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py#L1896-L2033> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match-3> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "docs/media/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling_comparison.png (generated output)" ;
        dct:description "3 x 3 synthesis figure: A-F Pass 2 panels, G spine closure sweep, H chip/repair kymograph, I repair-outcome phase diagram — docs/media/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling_comparison.png: rendered output of 2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py at e651a8b8, image/png, 1511143 B, 2454×2172 px, artifact_sha256 9a3f32d98065e16f7fa63f39ab8a2b61e070b482616d8e3ef280efaef20643a0 (sha256 9a3f32d98065e16f7fa63f39ab8a2b61e070b482616d8e3ef280efaef20643a0), spec_fingerprint 5ce4d2a0cdd2530a2bb4e03307b8a1565e305db6cf6b377ff8cb6db26ef82d9e" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match-4> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "docs/media/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling_spine_closure_repair_3d.png (generated output)" ;
        dct:description "New 3D figure: stacked spine cross-sections forming a hollow tube; chipped valve with repaired ribs in register — docs/media/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling_spine_closure_repair_3d.png: rendered output of 2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py at e651a8b8, image/png, 444536 B, 1516×717 px, artifact_sha256 24dc99868357964d8a64afc070baa971eb8a1ed951f4e6287114529612b7f832 (sha256 24dc99868357964d8a64afc070baa971eb8a1ed951f4e6287114529612b7f832), spec_fingerprint 5ce4d2a0cdd2530a2bb4e03307b8a1565e305db6cf6b377ff8cb6db26ef82d9e" .
